module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CartesianImpliesQuasicoherent

/-!
# Cartesian on affine charts implies quasi-coherent on the small étale site

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let `G` be
an `𝒪_F`-module on the small étale site of `F` which is *cartesian on affine charts*
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts`): for every morphism of affine étale charts
the sections over the smaller chart are the base change of the sections over the larger one.
**This file proves that such a module is quasi-coherent on the site**, which is one of the two
implications of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2).

`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CartesianImpliesQuasicoherent` had reduced that implication
to a single hypothesis: over an affine étale chart `V`, the *relations* among the canonical
generating family `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGenerators` — whose being an epimorphism is
proved there — must themselves be generated by global ones, i.e. the kernel of the generating
family must receive an epimorphism from a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf of the slice
at `V`.  That is the hypothesis `hrel` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_rel`, and it is
discharged here.

The relations morphism is indexed by *all* the relations among the tautological generators, so
nothing has to be chosen; what has to be proved is that it is onto the kernel, and that is a
statement about sections over the affine objects of the slice, where three inputs meet:

* the sections of the generating coproduct over an affine object of the slice are the finitely
  supported families of regular functions on it — Stacks 0935(2) at the presentation universe;
* the restriction map of regular functions between affine étale charts is flat
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine`); and
* the sections of `G` over the smaller chart are the base change of the sections over the larger
  one, which is the cartesian hypothesis.

Flatness turns the second and third into "the relations base change too", and that is the
commutative-algebra core of the file.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.familySectionsMap` is the comparison map `(I →₀ E(X)) ⟶ P(X)` attached to a
  family `ι : ∀ i : I, E ⟶ P` of morphisms of sheaves of modules: the `R(X)`-linear map sending
  `Finsupp.single i x` to the image of `x` under `ι i`.  For `E` the structure sheaf and `P`
  Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.free I` it is `Stacks.Sites.freeSectionsMap`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartUnitSection` reads a regular function on a chart as a global
  section of the structure sheaf of the slice at that chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratorsCombination` evaluates a finitely supported family of
  regular functions on a chart at the tautological generating family of `G` over it, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRelationsIndex` is the kernel of that map: the module of
  relations among the generators.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRelationsSource`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRelationsLeg` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRelations` are the coproduct of copies of
  `SheafOfModules.liftUnitPresentation` indexed by those relations, the leg of the canonical
  morphism at a coefficient family, and the morphism itself.  This is the arbitrary-index
  analogue of `SheafOfModules.powRel`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratorsCoeffMap` is the comparison from the finitely supported
  families of regular functions on an object of the slice to the sections of the generating
  coproduct over it, as a *linear* map.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.bijective_familySectionsMap`: **the sections over a quasi-compact object of a
  coproduct of copies of a sheaf of modules are the finitely supported families of sections of
  that sheaf.**  This is Stacks 0935(2) read on an abstract colimiting cofan instead of on
  `SheafOfModules.free`, so it applies at any module universe and to a coproduct of copies of
  the *universe-lifted* structure sheaf `SheafOfModules.liftUnit`, which is the one a global
  presentation takes.  `Stacks.Sites.bijective_freeSectionsMap` is its case
  `E = SheafOfModules.unit R`, `P = SheafOfModules.free I`; it is not re-derived from it here,
  because it lives upstream of this file, as the two cases of
  `SheafOfModules.hasFiniteGlobalPresentation_of_isFiniteFree` recorded in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteLocallyFreeCoherent` are not.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_chartGeneratorsSectionsMap`: the same statement for the
  coproduct `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratorsSource` over an affine object of the slice,
  the quasi-compactness being
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompactObject_over_of_isAffine`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_eq_span_image_mapRange_of_flat`: **the relations among a
  generating family base change along a flat ring map.**  Let `A → A'` be flat, let
  `φ₀ : (I →₀ A) ⟶ M₀` and `φ₁ : (I →₀ A') ⟶ M₁` be presented by one index type, and let `M₁`
  receive the base change `A' ⊗_A M₀` injectively and compatibly.  Then the kernel of `φ₁` is
  generated over `A'` by the restrictions of the relations among the generators of `M₀`.  This is
  the commutative-algebra content of the relations half of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2), and it is
  the companion of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.bijective_baseChange_of_exact` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChartSectionsKernel`, which is the same argument for the
  *kernel* rather than for the span of the relations.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRelations_comp_chartGenerators`: the two morphisms of the
  canonical presentation compose to zero, over an arbitrary chart.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_range_chartRelations_val_app`: **every relation among the chart
  generators, over an affine object of the slice, is in the range of the relations morphism.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_kernelLift_chartRelations`: **the relations among the chart
  generators are generated by global ones**, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_chartRelations_epi_kernelLift`, which is the hypothesis `hrel`
  of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_rel`
  discharged.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_anyUniverse`: **a
  module cartesian on affine charts is quasi-coherent on the small étale site**, unconditionally
  and at any universe of module sections;
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts` is the case of
  sections in the universe of the schemes.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.Sites.familySectionsMap` is stated with the index type in the module universe, as
`Stacks.Sites.freeSectionsMap` is, but for a different reason: there the pin is Mathlib's, because
`SheafOfModules.free` exists only for `I` in the universe of the coefficient rings, whereas here
it is bookkeeping in `ModuleCat.of` — the finitely supported families `I →₀ E(X)` live in
`Type (max w s)` for `I : Type w` and sections in `Type s`, so they are the sections of a module
only when `w ≤ s`.  `Stacks.Sites.sheafOfModules_sections_preserves_coproducts`, the input, has
the index universe free.  At the small étale site of an algebraic space over `Scheme.{u}` the
presentation universe of an `𝒪_F`-module with sections in `m` is `max (u + 1) m` and the index
types of the canonical generating family and of the relations are both in `Type (max (u + 1) m)`,
so the restriction is satisfied where it is used.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ker_eq_span_image_mapRange_of_flat` takes its comparison map as an
*additive* map and not as a linear one.  Only additivity is used, and the comparison the
application has is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.sectionsBaseChange`, whose linearity is over the
larger of the two rings only.  The three universes of its modules are free, and its instance
binders are named, because the application supplies them explicitly; see the next paragraph.

**The two spellings of the ring of regular functions on an object of a slice, and what it costs.**
For an object `Z` of the slice of the small étale site at a chart `V`, the ring
`((RingedSite.ringSheaf …).over V).obj.obj (op Z)` and the ring
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing … Z.left` are *definitionally equal* but not syntactically so,
and instance search crosses the gap in neither direction:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartRing_commRing`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartAlgebra` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.moduleFlat_chartRing_of_isAffine` are stated for an object of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SmallEtale` and are *not* found at a goal
phrased with the projection `.C` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallEtaleRingedSite`, while the
module structures on the sections of a sheaf on the slice are found only in the slice spelling.
Three devices appear below and each is load-bearing:

* the flat base change lemma is applied with its commutative-ring, algebra and flatness instances
  **passed by name**, which is why its instance binders carry names;
* every statement that mixes the two spellings is applied in **term** mode, where unification is
  up to definitional equality, rather than by `rw`, which matches syntactically — `rw` reports a
  pattern as absent from a goal that displays it verbatim, with the "not type-correct under the
  `implicit` transparency level" note, exactly here; and
* where a scalar coming from the chart spelling has to act on sections in the slice spelling,
  it is written `@id` of the slice spelling, which is definitionally the identity and gives the
  term the syntactic type the scalar action needs.  A type ascription does *not* work for a local
  hypothesis: the elaborator keeps the declared type.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratorsCoeffMap` is a `LinearMap` and not a bare function for the
same reason: its additivity and homogeneity, which the span induction in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_range_chartRelations_val_app` needs, are then `map_add` and
`map_smul` rather than three `Finsupp.ext` computations, each of which forced the elaborator
through the two spellings and overran the heartbeat limit.

**No `set_option` of any kind appears in this file**, and none is needed.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute is claimed.**  Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) is an equivalence of
categories in the Descent chapter (Chapter 35), and only one of its two
implications is proved here; the converse is carried as the hypothesis `hEss` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_essSurj` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SliceAssociatedModuleEssSurj`.  The convention of the
sibling files `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CartesianImpliesQuasicoherent` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FreeModuleCartesian` is followed.

